Proposed (19.3s): Use this skill whenever the user reports or wants to debug an audio problem in the ttaccessible / TeamTalk app — symptoms involving the mic, speakers, AEC / echo cancellation, hearing their own echo, voice leaking to other users in a channel, VoiceOver bleeding into the mic, no sound reaching the channel even when mic preview works, crackling / distortion / saturation on a USB interface, hot-plug or device-switch glitches, mic preview freeze, sample-rate mismatches, or AVAudioEngine / AUHAL failures. Trigger on symptom descriptions in any language (English, French, etc.) — the user does NOT need to say "log", "AEC diag", or any technical term; "j'entends mon écho", "mon micro grésille", "AEC isn't cancelling", "others hear my speakers" all qualify. Reads `~/Library/Logs/TTAccessible/audio.log` (wiped each launch — reproduce first) with ready-made grep patterns. Do NOT use for code refactors, unit tests, UI tweaks, SDK questions, or AEC theory.

